==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|firezzan|lang=goh}}, {{term|frezzan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|fraetaną|lang=gem-pro}}. Cognate with Danish {{term|fråse|lang=da}}, Gothic {{term|𐍆𐍂𐌰𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌽|tr=fraitan|lang=got}}, English {{term|fret|lang=en}}.

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=5|frisst|fraß|gefressen|past subjunctive=fräße}}

# {{intransitive|of an animal}} to [[eat]]; to [[feed]]
# {{intransitive|of a person|colloquial|lang=de}} to [[stuff]] oneself; to [[gorge]] oneself; to [[eat]] like a pig
# {{transitive|of an animal}} to [[devour]]; to [[eat]] (something)
# {{transitive|of a person|colloquial|lang=de}} to [[stuff]] oneself on (something); to [[gorge]] on (something)
# {{transitive|colloquial|figuratively|lang=de}} to [[guzzle]] (e.g. gas); to [[burn]] through (e.g. money)

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj-strong|fress|fraß|gefressen|h||friss|fräß|a|a|||a}}

====Usage notes====
{{term|fressen|Fressen}} contrasts with the more refined {{term|essen||to eat}}.

